    contentS: '# Termux Automation Scripts\n' +
      '\n' +
      'This repository contains a collection of bash scripts that automate various tasks in the Termux terminal environment. These scripts are designed to simplify repetitive tasks, making Termux usage more efficient.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Features\n' +
      '\n' +
      '- **Bash Script Registration**: Automate the process of registering and setting up bash scripts for easy global access.\n' +
      '- **`.gitignore` Generator**: Quickly generate a `.gitignore` file for different languages and frameworks.\n' +
      '- **Additional Automations**: More scripts for common tasks in Termux will be added over time.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Installation\n' +
      '\n' +
      '1. Clone the repository to your Termux environment:\n' +
      '\n' +
      '   ```bash\n' +
      '   git clone https://github.com/Chaos-19/termux-scripts.git\n' +
      '   cd termux-scripts\n' +
      '   ```\n' +
      '\n' +
      '2. Make sure the scripts are executable:\n' +
      '\n' +
      '   ```bash\n' +
      '   chmod +x *.sh\n' +
      '   ```\n' +
      '\n' +
      '3. Add the repository to your `PATH` to access the scripts globally:\n' +
      '\n' +
      '   ```bash\n' +
      `   echo 'export PATH="$HOME/termux-scripts:$PATH"' >> ~/.bashrc\n` +
      '   source ~/.bashrc\n' +
      '   ```\n' +
      '\n' +
      '4. Now you can run the scripts from anywhere in Termux.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Available Scripts\n' +
      '\n' +
      '### 1. Bash Script Registration (`register-script.sh`)\n' +
      '\n' +
      'This script automates the process of making a bash script globally accessible in the Termux environment by adding it to your `$PATH` and ensuring it is executable.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '#### Usage:\n' +
      '\n' +
      '```bash\n' +
      './register-script.sh /path/to/your-script.sh\n' +
      '```\n' +
      '\n' +
      'This will:\n' +
      '- Ensure the script is executable.\n' +
      "- Add the script's directory to the global `$PATH`.\n" +
      '\n' +
      '### 2. `.gitignore` Generator (`generate-gitignore.sh`)\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Automatically generate a `.gitignore` file tailored for a specific language or framework.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '#### Usage:\n' +
      '\n' +
      '```bash\n' +
      './generate-gitignore.sh nodejs  # For a Node.js project\n' +
      '```\n' +
      '\n' +
      'The script will fetch the appropriate `.gitignore` template and save it to your current working directory.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '### 3. Custom Scripts\n' +
      '\n' +
      'This section will be updated as more scripts are added.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Contributing\n' +
      '\n' +
      "Feel free to submit a pull request if you have a useful automation script you'd like to add. Make sure to include documentation for your script in the `README.md`.\n" +
      '\n' +
